module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.WordTraps

/-!
# Traps for 57 blocks of period 11, from walls of period eleven carried leftward

The natural scan of periods 10 to 12 finds that the commonest traps at period 11 are walls of 16 cells, the closures of
the true windows of right halves driven by `00000011011`, `00110100111` and `00001101001` at step 12,000, whose chains
become periodic in the distance, as the wall of period 10 does in [TenTraps](TenTraps.md). Carried leftward up to 40
columns, they give traps to 57 blocks of period 11 that the kit does not exclude, each at the first wall and the least
distance that reaches it. The third wall reaches no block that the first two do not.

* `elevenTraps`, `elevenTraps_check`: the traps, all passing the check of [WordTraps](WordTraps.md).
* `elevenTraps_blocks`: their blocks.
* `eleven_absorption_excludes`: for each of them, if every finitely supported right half driven by the block
  enters its trap, the center column does not eventually repeat the block.

The tables come from `python -m computations.lock_chain --lean-walls 11`. The natural-language argument is
`ElevenTraps.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata

